{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0369", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "MATH_0002": "$S' \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "MATH_0005": "$S'$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "MATH_0007": "$S' \\to S$", "MATH_0008": "$S'$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "MATH_0010": "$S$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-descending-properties}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-syntomic-flat}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-syntomic-locally-finite-presentation}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-Noetherian-local-fppf}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{coherent-definition-depth}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-Sk-goes-up}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-syntomic-characterize}", "REF_0008": "\\ref{algebra-definition-lci}", "REF_0009": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-lci-CM}", "REF_0010": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-descent-Sk}", "REF_0011": "\\ref{lemma-descending-properties}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1161b0262695760e5a074768286ba2c28d47931dd9daccc7a82448ab30a2e60d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3e2477decde665270ff643676cdc858e295fd5e2351b4d3839a8033db69ee03e", "source_text": "We will check (1), (2) and (3) of Lemma <REF_0001>.\nAs a syntomic morphism is flat of finite presentation\n(Morphisms, Lemmas <REF_0002>\nand <REF_0003>)\nwe have already checked this for ``being locally Noetherian'' in the proof\nof Lemma <REF_0004>.\nWe will use this without further mention in the proof.\nFirst we note that <MATH_0001> is local in the Zariski topology.\nThis is clear from the definition,\nsee Cohomology of Schemes, Definition <REF_0005>.\nNext, we show that if <MATH_0002> is a syntomic morphism of affines\nand <MATH_0003> has <MATH_0004>, then <MATH_0005> has <MATH_0006>. This\nis Algebra, Lemma <REF_0006>\n(use\nMorph